{"_v":1,"id":"arcadia-2011","cs":78,"rc":11,"bd":{"positive":7,"mixed":4,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Terry Teachout","o":"The Wall Street Journal","s":95,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.wsj.com/articles/SB10001424052748703959604576204962051751690","d":"2011-03-18","q":"Tom Stoppard's 'Arcadia' is arguably the finest play by a living dramatist, a work that manages to be simultaneously profound and entertaining, intellectually rigorous and emotionally satisfying."},{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":88,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://www.nytimes.com/2011/03/18/theater/reviews/arcadia-by-tom-stoppard-on-broadway-review.html","d":"2011-03-17","q":"This is as entertaining as it is enlightening, a rare combination that justifies the recent revival's move to Broadway."},{"cn":"Marilyn Stasio","o":"Variety","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"http://www.variety.com/review/VE1117944840?categoryid=33&amp;cs=1&amp;cmpid=RSS|News|LatestNews","d":"2011-03-17","q":"On this level alone, the play is an enchantment."},{"cn":"Linda Winer","o":"Newsday","s":82,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://www.newsday.com/news/new-york/theater-review-arcadia-3-5-stars-t20271","q":"Arcadia is a heady, aching thrill of a tragicomedy."},{"cn":"Scott Brown","o":"Vulture","s":79,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"https://nymag.com/daily/entertainment/2011/03/stage_dive_an_exquisite_reviva.html","d":"2011-03-17","q":"Seldom has a more romantic finale been more rationally, stealthily staged–the impact sneaks up on you."},{"cn":"David Rooney","o":"The Hollywood Reporter","s":63,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-reviews/arcadia-theater-review-168928/","d":"2011-03-17","q":"That’s too infrequently the case with this uneven cast."},{"cn":"Elisabeth Vincentelli","o":"New York Post","s":59,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"http://www.nypost.com/p/entertainment/theater/the_tedium_is_the_message_in_tangled_Q0IC1kUiMoTbGmQGPwZDwK#ixzz1Gy9Ja8gz","d":"2011-03-17","q":"It's easy to admire, but hard to love."},{"cn":"Melissa Rose Bernardo","o":"Entertainment Weekly","s":90,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://ew.com/article/2011/03/18/this-week-on-stage-fat-pig-arcadia/?srsltid=AfmBOori3w79lUxN4ektrLcCFXWU9sCuwk6kf7GI2tujF2t4rU1sofWD","d":"2011-03-18","q":"She raves 'the acting could hardly be better … personally I preferred this cast to the original production's' and gives it an A-."},{"cn":"Matthew Murray","o":"Talkin' Broadway","s":83,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"https://www.talkinbroadway.com/world/Arcadia.html","d":"2011-03-20","q":"This production of Arcadia succeeds because it finds the perfect balance between Stoppard's intellectual complexity and his emotional accessibility."},{"cn":"Erik Haagensen","o":"Backstage","s":70,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"https://www.backstage.com/bso/content_display/reviews/ny-theatre-reviews/e3ifb5e4ab05dc798b739fc7d8129188c75","q":"It may be Stoppard's best play, and even an indistinct production can't subdue its poignancy and wisdom."},{"cn":"Michael Sommers","o":"New Jersey Newsroom","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":3,"u":"https://www.newjerseynewsroom.com/movies/review-arcadia-speaks-indistinctly-about-past-lives-and-loves","q":"Keeping the play's underlying emotions rather on the cool side, Leveaux grievously errs by usually pacing the conversations at a hasty clip."}],"au":{"score":73,"designation":"Shrugging","sources":{"mz":{"s":66,"c":21,"sr":3.3},"ss":{"s":76,"c":44},"th":{"s":80,"c":5}}},"hi":"/images/shows/arcadia-2011/hero.png","ta":"243 W 47th St, New York, NY 10036","pd":"2011-02-26","ca":[{"n":"Margaret Colin","r":"Lady Croom"},{"n":"Billy Crudup","r":"Bernard Nightingale"},{"n":"Raúl Esparza","r":"Valentine Coverly"},{"n":"Glenn Fleshler","r":"Captain Brice, RN"},{"n":"Grace Gummer","r":"Chloë Coverly"},{"n":"Edward James Hyland","r":"Jellaby"},{"n":"Byron Jennings","r":"Richard Noakes"},{"n":"Bel Powley","r":"Thomasina Coverly"},{"n":"Tom Riley","r":"Septimus Hodge"},{"n":"Noah Robbins","r":"Gus Coverly"},{"n":"David Turner","r":"Ezra Chater"},{"n":"Lia Williams","r":"Hannah Jarvis"}]}